==Plot==
<!---As per [[MOS:TVPLOT]], season summaries should each be a maximum 100 words--->
In the [[Gotham season 1|first season]], [[Gotham City Police Department|GCPD]] Detective [[James Gordon (Gotham)|James Gordon]] and his partially corrupt partner [[Harvey Bullock (Gotham)|Harvey Bullock]] are tasked with solving a number of criminal cases in [[Gotham City]], including the murder of 12-year-old [[Bruce Wayne (Gotham)|Bruce Wayne]]'s parents. A gang war brews between crime families led by [[Carmine Falcone]], [[Sal Maroni]], and [[Fish Mooney]], with low-level thug [[Oswald Cobblepot (Gotham)|Oswald Cobblepot]] forced into its center.

In the [[Gotham season 2|second season]], [[Theo Galavan]] surfaces in Gotham to kill Bruce Wayne for the [[List of criminal organizations in DC Comics#O|Order of St. Dumas]]; Gordon is framed for murder by [[Edward Nygma (Gotham)|Edward Nygma]]; and at [[Arkham Asylum]], Professor [[Hugo Strange]] runs unorthodox experiments in a secret facility called Indian Hill, transforming its inmates into monsters for the mysterious [[Court of Owls]].

In the [[Gotham season 3|third season]], Gordon becomes a bounty hunter working to track down the Indian Hill monsters. [[Jervis Tetch (Gotham)|Jervis Tetch]] threatens the city's safety with a deadly virus; Cobblepot and Nygma struggle for control over Gotham; and Bruce is told by the Court of Owls' [[Sensei (DC Comics)|leader]] to seek out [[Ra's al Ghul (Gotham)|Ra's al Ghul]] to complete his training.

In the [[Gotham season 4|fourth season]], Bruce begins to fight crime as a masked vigilante tentatively named the "Dark Knight" to prepare for Ra's al Ghul's return; [[Sofia Falcone (Gotham)|Sofia Falcone]] arrives in Gotham to reclaim the criminal underworld from Cobblepot, who has established a new law of "licensed crime"; and [[Jerome and Jeremiah Valeska|Jeremiah Valeska]] is driven insane and forms an alliance with Ra's al Ghul to turn the city into an [[Batman: No Man's Land|isolated ruin]], forcing Bruce to fulfill his destiny as "Gotham's Dark Knight".

In the [[Gotham season 5|fifth and final season]], Gordon and his allies attempt to restore order in Gotham. [[Nyssa al Ghul (Gotham)|Nyssa al Ghul]] seeks vengeance for her father's death; [[Eduardo Dorrance]] takes control of the city's military presence; and Jeremiah hatches a scheme to torment Bruce and cement their "bond" as hated enemies.

A [[The Beginning...|decade later]], Bruce returns to Gotham, which has flourished with Gordon as commissioner of the GCPD, and begins fighting crime as a [[Batman|bat-inspired vigilante]], capturing Cobblepot and Nygma after both attempt to kill Gordon. Jeremiah, having feigned [[brain death]] during this time, escapes from Arkham to resume his rivalry with Bruce, but is captured by him soon after, starting animosity between Jeremiah and Bruce's alter-egos. Gordon decides against retirement and uses a [[Bat-Signal|searchlight]] atop the police department to contact the new vigilante.

